1
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,860
He had been like this for a while.

2
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:36,140
He once said, Don't just let
any random object into the house.

3
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,820
And don't pick up any
strange things around the house.

4
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:43,020
Because the criminals that
he caught are plotting revenge.

5
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:47,780
He’s locked himself in the prayer room
and hasn't come down for a while now.

6
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:49,820
Just sitting there, chanting.

7
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,620
And lately.

8
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:58,820
There are strange noises upstairs.
Doesn't sound like him.

9
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:15,340
I called the Headman
and told him what's going on.

10
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:17,980
He's certain it's a curse.

11
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:22,420
He's taking me
to the shaman at the market.

12
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:27,100
I'll tell him what's going on.
Maybe he'll come do the ritual here.

13
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:31,780
Oh.

14
00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:34,420
I have to hang up, Tuk.
The Headman's here to pick me up.

15
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:36,180
Okay, okay.

16
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:39,300
Singha.

17
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:42,420
I have to go out. I'll be right back.

18
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,900
If there's an emergency,
call Uncle Non at his house.

19
00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:49,820
Run away.

20
00:02:58,010 --> 00:02:58,980
Run away.

21
00:02:59,490 --> 00:03:01,900
Run away. Run away.

22
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:18,340
Auntie, glass noodle salad,
blue crabs, papaya salad, and two beers.

23
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,020
They want a discount on the chair fee.

24
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:24,580
Said there's a lot of them.
Complained that it's too expensive.

25
00:04:24,810 --> 00:04:26,460
Ugh, hell no! No discount!

26
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:28,580
Don't like it?
Go sit somewhere else then.

27
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:31,220
Do they have any idea
how much I pay the mafia?

28
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:33,140
I can't say a damn thing.

29
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:34,900
Okay, I'm on it.

30
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,860
That guy is so annoying.

31
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,260
Hey, Foon.

32
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,900
Where are Singha and his guys?

33
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:20,340
Wow, holding her.
Zero respect for the husband.

34
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,420
Hmm.

35
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:31,460
you and your wife have a party.

36
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,460
Party at tonight.

37
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:35,180
Five o'clock.

38
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:40,100
I'll drive around and
pick you up at the hotel. Okay?

39
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,660
Ok. no problem.

40
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,020
- Where's the stuff?
- Oh.

41
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:46,820
Where's the stuff?

42
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,020
Damn. His Thai is better than mine.

43
00:05:50,570 --> 00:05:53,140
No wonder he understood my gibberish.

44
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,460
Money, Money.

45
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:01,460
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much. see you tonight.

46
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:04,020
Ok, Happy, happy.

47
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:06,060
- See you.
- Ok, See you.

48
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:08,100
Gonna go back and get some.

49
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:11,020
Hey, Singha.

50
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:14,260
This group is fucking easy.
The bastards aren't fussy at all.

51
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:17,100
- Easy, my ass.
- Hm!

52
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:18,580
Lately, these assholes are getting smart.

53
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:20,380
- Taking videos and shit.
- Ah!

54
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:22,420
Tonight, take all their fucking phones.

55
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,940
- Understood?
- Yeah, I get it. No need to teach me.

56
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,180
Ouch!

57
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,620
Just let me have a body like yours.
I'll get you back.

58
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,820
Anything else?

59
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:48,300
Joe.

60
00:06:49,130 --> 00:06:51,260
- Why? Afraid you'll forget it?
- Yeah.

61
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:53,660
Here, Mom.

62
00:06:54,210 --> 00:06:55,340
Oh, Thanks a lot.

63
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:57,100
Lock the door tonight, Mom.

64
00:06:57,770 --> 00:06:59,980
I'm sleeping at Tun's shop
with Joe tonight.

65
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:03,980
- You should keep some for yourself.
- You keep it, Mom.

66
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:07,020
Don't worry about him.
He'll make some more tonight.

67
00:07:07,330 --> 00:07:09,860
- Girls are all over him.
- Don't listen to her, Mom.

68
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:11,780
Big tips.

69
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:14,100
like they're taking Singha home
for the night.

70
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:18,220
Damn. How come nobody
ever wants to buy me out?

71
00:07:18,970 --> 00:07:20,220
With a face like yours?

72
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:22,940
- Hey, you never know.
- Just go to sleep.

73
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:24,140
- Foreigners like exotic stuff.
- Go to sleep.

74
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,340
Enough, You guys stay and
help my mom with the beach chairs.

75
00:07:27,910 --> 00:07:29,540
I'll deal with the Sergeant first.

76
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:32,540
So they won't be poking
around Tun's shop tonight.

77
00:07:34,730 --> 00:07:37,700
Don't forget your medicine
tonight, Mom. Take it before bed.

78
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,500
Yeah, I won't forget.

79
00:07:41,490 --> 00:07:42,300
Bye.

80
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,820
- You don't know anything.
- Go get...

81
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,340
Singha only made 1,500.
But I got mine yesterday.

82
00:07:47,490 --> 00:07:48,180
- Hey!
- So how much did you get?

83
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,540
- Why are you guys even arguing?
- It's 1,900. Plus a free lunch box.

84
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,780
- Seriously, are you gonna keep arguing all day?
- You get fed, too.

85
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,180
He's just a big talker.

86
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:20,540
Hey, what the fuck are you guys doing?

87
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,860
Ganging up on a defenseless guy, huh?

88
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,700
What the fuck does this
have to do with you? Huh?

89
00:08:29,410 --> 00:08:30,620
You piece of shit.

90
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:49,820
You.

91
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,860
Are you okay?

92
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,660
Umm.

93
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,060
Are you okay?

94
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:13,540
You bastard!

95
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:18,020
Hey! You.

96
00:09:18,610 --> 00:09:19,260
Hey.

97
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:21,020
Aren't you dead yet?

98
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:22,460
What's the hell?

99
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:27,700
Police!

100
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,460
- Here is your Blue Hawaii.
- Thank you.

101
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,620
Here I am. Oh.

102
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,780
Family favorite!
Here, take one each.

103
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,460
Thank you.

104
00:10:35,850 --> 00:10:36,620
Hey.

105
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,860
I talked to Singha. We’re done dealing.

106
00:10:44,290 --> 00:10:45,100
Damn.

107
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:49,020
What's gotten into you?
Suddenly want to be a saint?

108
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:51,020
Just thinking.

109
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:53,300
It's Singha.

110
00:10:53,730 --> 00:10:56,220
He says the cops are starting
to sniff around.

111
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:58,620
Besides, there are a lot of
new drug dealers.

112
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:01,980
I'm not looking to sit behind bars
twiddling my thumbs.

113
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,380
I'm scared of prison, man.

114
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:05,940
So what are you guys going to do next?

115
00:11:07,690 --> 00:11:08,380
There.

116
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:09,900
Ask Mr. Singha over there.

117
00:11:10,970 --> 00:11:11,940
Isn't that right, Mr. Singha?

118
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:13,500
My friend Singha.

119
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:15,300
Little bro Singha!

120
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:16,900
Singha, you bastard!

121
00:11:17,190 --> 00:11:18,860
- Huh? What?
- What the hell?

122
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:23,260
Tell her what we would do
if we weren't selling drugs.

123
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:27,500
Joe and I have been thinking
about it for a long time.

124
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:30,060
That once we save up enough money,

125
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,140
we'll open a bar
on the beach over there.

126
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:40,060
I already told Mr. Chatch
that I'm going to quit.

127
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:46,660
Is Mr. Chatch
gonna let you quit that easily?

128
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,540
He said it himself.

129
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,700
He’s letting another dealer
take care of it.

130
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,900
Seems like it’s those
new politicians who just stepped in.

131
00:11:57,090 --> 00:11:58,180
They’re gonna deal it themselves.

132
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:02,420
Well, I hope it works out for you. Cheers!

133
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:04,380
One sip and you're already drunk?

134
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:07,260
I'm not buying this brand anymore.

135
00:12:07,970 --> 00:12:08,620
Singha.

136
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,060
Are you okay?

137
00:12:12,490 --> 00:12:13,700
Yes, I’m Okay.

138
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:15,540
- You’re okay?
- you okay.

139
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:21,420
Using a toast as a signal?
You’re a crafty one, tiger.

140
00:12:21,650 --> 00:12:23,460
Setting the bait
for another deer again, I see.

141
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,420
And it’s not even a Thai deer.
It’s a reindeer straight-up imported.

142
00:12:28,170 --> 00:12:30,060
Hey, is she a fortune teller?

143
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,060
- Watch my leg, man!
- That Sing guy or something?

144
00:12:32,330 --> 00:12:33,740
You idiot! Hey, wait a minute!

145
00:12:34,070 --> 00:12:35,380
You two know each other that well?

146
00:12:43,950 --> 00:12:45,660
Cheers!

147
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:49,820
- Papi, I'm so cold.
- Alright, come here, baby.

148
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,580
- Cheers!
- Cheers! Cheers!

149
00:12:54,670 --> 00:12:57,740
Boss, there's an MP candidate
asking to see you.

150
00:12:57,970 --> 00:12:59,500
- Let him in.
- Yes, sir.

151
00:13:00,410 --> 00:13:01,300
Come in.

152
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:09,260
Hello, Sir.

153
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,660
My name is Arnon Suphanpon.

154
00:13:11,890 --> 00:13:13,020
Candidate number two.

155
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,900
If I make any mistakes.

156
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:19,260
Please let me know, P'Akkharaphon.

157
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:21,700
Drop the 'P'. I'm not your brother.

158
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:24,300
I'm older than your father.

159
00:13:25,450 --> 00:13:26,700
What right do you have.

160
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:28,860
To compete with me?

161
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:30,740
You little punk!

162
00:13:31,970 --> 00:13:34,580
You’re standing over me.
Get down here!

163
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:37,660
Get the hell down!

164
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:38,900
Yes, sir.

165
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,460
Don't you know a damn thing?

166
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:51,980
Who runs this place!

167
00:13:52,850 --> 00:13:53,860
Do you have any idea.

168
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,420
What happened to the person
who applied before you?

169
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,980
He's pissing me off.

170
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,620
The next day,

171
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:03,980
I dumped his ass in the ocean.

172
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:05,740
Yes.

173
00:14:06,670 --> 00:14:09,700
So, I intended to come
and pay my respects to you.

174
00:14:10,330 --> 00:14:12,620
Stop talking. I'm not finished.

175
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,140
This town is mine.

176
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,060
Wait until I'm dead.

177
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:19,420
Then you can have your little thoughts.

178
00:14:22,210 --> 00:14:24,460
I don't know what the hell
they're having an election for.

179
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,500
I'm winning anyway.

180
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,220
Who the hell do you work for?

181
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,060
I have no master.

182
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:35,060
I grew up all on my own, sir.

183
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:39,060
My father took his own life,
and my mother followed suit.

184
00:14:39,850 --> 00:14:41,780
Spent two years
drifting in and out of psych wards.

185
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:49,260
Keep going until I tell you to stop.

186
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:51,780
Papi, Let me refill your glass.
It’s almost empty.

187
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:54,060
But I’m all better now, sir.

188
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,300
I have to make progress on my own, sir.

189
00:14:56,520 --> 00:15:00,820
I work hard, I search,
and I do whatever it takes.

190
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:02,540
And if there's something I can't do,

191
00:15:03,290 --> 00:15:04,700
I hire someone to get it done.

192
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:12,620
I just want to help
the people of this city, sir.

193
00:15:14,130 --> 00:15:16,420
Whatever they can't do,
I want to do it for them.

194
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:18,940
All I'm asking for is a chance.

195
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,100
I have no intention
of stepping on your toes.

196
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:22,500
Tomorrow.

197
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:26,420
Pull your name out of this competition,
and mark my words!

198
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:29,180
Don't ever show your face here again.
Leave!

199
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:34,220
- What are you waiting for? Get out!
- Yes, sir. Thank you.

200
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,820
- Papi, don't be so stressed.
- Get going. Now!

201
00:15:39,970 --> 00:15:41,900
- Yes.
- Let's have a drink.

202
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:48,020
Finish your glass.

203
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:52,220
Very good.

204
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:57,620
Hey, whose hair is this?

205
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,580
It feels like freaking broken glass! Huh!?

206
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,180
If I have to wait for you to die.

207
00:16:38,170 --> 00:16:39,220
Then, I'm waiting.

208
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:26,340
It's coming!

209
00:17:27,410 --> 00:17:28,700
Run away.

210
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:29,780
Hey.

211
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:29,820
- Yes.
- Hey, Serge.

212
00:18:30,890 --> 00:18:32,420
According to eyewitnesses.

213
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:34,660
the Mayor’s close subordinate.

214
00:18:34,970 --> 00:18:37,740
Said he looked like
he couldn't breathe before he passed away.

215
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:40,100
But noted there were two
or three hostesses present.

216
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:41,820
Who were constantly
pouring drinks for the Mayor.

217
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:48,420
And where are the hostesses now?

218
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,860
They’ve all run away, sir.

219
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:54,220
Oh, but before that.

220
00:18:54,450 --> 00:18:55,700
The subordinates also mentioned that.

221
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:59,940
Mr. Arnon, candidate number two,
who’s running against the Mayor.

222
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:01,260
came to see him,

223
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:03,420
but left before the incident occurred.

224
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:08,860
Bring in all those girls for interrogation.

225
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,060
And get Arnon too.

226
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:11,700
Yes, sir.

227
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:17,900
Three female bodies were
found lying dead on the beach.

228
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,580
It looks like they’ve been dead
for a long time.

229
00:19:29,290 --> 00:19:30,380
That's all for today.

230
00:19:36,770 --> 00:19:37,820
Are you going to eat something first?

231
00:19:37,930 --> 00:19:39,700
- No.
- Then hurry up.

232
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:51,460
- Mom...
- Hey.

233
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:53,500
- Oh.
- No need to call her, stay still.

234
00:20:01,050 --> 00:20:01,820
Fuck.

235
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:03,980
The city page posted it this morning.

236
00:20:04,210 --> 00:20:06,940
The mayor just checked in
with the Grim Reaper.

237
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:08,980
Holy crap, and they found
a woman's body in the sea too.

238
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:09,980
Holy shit!

239
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:12,140
It's a 'Death-Deaf' situation.

240
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,020
Holy shit, that’s so scary. Look at this!

241
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:19,260
Joe.

242
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:22,180
I think once we're done with
today's deliveries, we'd better to stop.

243
00:20:22,410 --> 00:20:24,500
The vibe in town is fucking weird lately.

244
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:26,660
Cops are all over the place.

245
00:20:28,690 --> 00:20:29,420
Yeah.

246
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:31,860
Alright, let me just finish
this batch first then.

247
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:33,820
Russia is fucking rushing me right now.

248
00:20:35,490 --> 00:20:36,740
Tun is already waiting for me up there.

249
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:37,860
I’m gonna go with him.

250
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:01,780
Oh! Hey.

251
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:06,700
Can I bum a cigarette?

252
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,060
What happened between you
and those guys last night?

253
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:27,380
It's an old rival.
Haven't seen them in a long time.

254
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:29,380
Those guys you saw are just his subordinates.

255
00:21:33,870 --> 00:21:36,340
Hey, about last night
when they shot at you.

256
00:21:37,690 --> 00:21:38,820
So, you didn't get hit, right?

257
00:21:39,610 --> 00:21:40,540
Nope, didn't get hit.

258
00:21:45,010 --> 00:21:46,220
Is your father's name It?

259
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:48,300
Whoa, hey!

260
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:50,300
Out of nowhere,
you asked for my father's name.

261
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:53,300
- What the hell is this?
- Born on the ninth.

262
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:54,620
September.

263
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:57,260
Whoa, who are you?

264
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:58,700
Are you a scammer?

265
00:21:59,810 --> 00:22:01,060
When did you see my card?

266
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,780
I think it’s time he came for you.

267
00:22:07,730 --> 00:22:09,100
Watch yourself.

268
00:22:10,330 --> 00:22:11,820
Stay away from the ones you love.

269
00:22:12,850 --> 00:22:13,980
Run if you can.

270
00:22:14,650 --> 00:22:15,660
Hide if you can.

271
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:18,540
This is the only warning I can give you.

272
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,300
What are you talking about?

273
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,980
Can I have a cigarette?

274
00:22:53,770 --> 00:22:55,740
I'm not cooking today. I'm exhausted.

275
00:22:56,290 --> 00:22:57,660
I’m not tired of the customers.

276
00:22:57,930 --> 00:22:59,700
Moving canvas chairs
with Foon was tried.

277
00:22:59,850 --> 00:23:01,020
It was just the two of us doing everything

278
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:03,180
I have no idea where Joe has disappeared to.

279
00:23:05,290 --> 00:23:06,020
Mom.

280
00:23:07,330 --> 00:23:08,460
Who is this guy?

281
00:23:08,900 --> 00:23:09,980
Mom, do you know him?

282
00:23:26,690 --> 00:23:27,540
His name. it's Dech.

283
00:23:28,250 --> 00:23:31,140
He’s a former Sergeant.
He used to work under your dad.

284
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:35,340
He's a fellow disciple of Khao Ao,
and he was an informant for his father.

285
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,860
Later on, I heard he moved to work
around the Suphanburi area.

286
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:41,540
Your father sent him to
investigate a case in Dan Chang.

287
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,500
Wait, so why didn't he come back
to work for his father again?

288
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:48,660
Your father told me that when he returned,

289
00:23:48,830 --> 00:23:51,140
Dech was rambling on about
being cursed with black magic.

290
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:55,260
It was those sorcerers
from the criminal's side.

291
00:23:55,540 --> 00:23:57,260
He said he was going to kill everyone.

292
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:00,260
He told your father to watch his back.

293
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:02,940
Not long after that, he just vanished

294
00:24:03,010 --> 00:24:04,780
maybe he didn't want to be
a burden to your father.

295
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:08,540
I only just ran into Dech
at the beginning of this year.

296
00:24:08,970 --> 00:24:11,900
He talks sense.
I give him empty bottles all the time.

297
00:24:14,070 --> 00:24:16,980
Mom, do you know what kind of case
he was investigating in Dan Chang?

298
00:24:17,250 --> 00:24:19,340
And what exactly was the conflict about?

299
00:24:20,210 --> 00:24:22,860
How should I know?
It's none of my business.

300
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:27,620
Hey, tomorrow I'm going to
have you take some fried squid.

301
00:24:27,890 --> 00:24:29,700
To the temple as an offering for the monk.

302
00:24:29,860 --> 00:24:32,580
They’re probably bored of eating
nothing but stir-fries and curries.

303
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:36,860
Sure, I'll take it there for you tomorrow.

304
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,060
Eat.

305
00:24:49,730 --> 00:24:51,220
Blessings to you.

306
00:24:52,770 --> 00:24:54,380
Hold the Phalo.
I need to watch my sugar right now.

307
00:24:57,470 --> 00:24:58,220
Oh.

308
00:25:03,290 --> 00:25:04,620
Please, brother.

309
00:25:05,450 --> 00:25:06,340
Please, teacher.

310
00:25:06,590 --> 00:25:08,660
Geez, Singha!

311
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:11,780
Just pick one. Is it Brother or teacher?

312
00:25:15,410 --> 00:25:19,300
What brought you here today?
Long time no see!

313
00:25:20,010 --> 00:25:21,980
Your house is practically next to the temple.

314
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,580
You even went to school here.

315
00:25:23,810 --> 00:25:26,900
yet it never crosses your mind
to come by and make some merit.

316
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:29,620
Huh, seems like only
your mother ever shows up.

317
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:34,340
Well, here I am. My mother sent me
to offer this fried squid to you, Bhante.

318
00:25:35,570 --> 00:25:36,540
Whoa!

319
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:37,260
Fried squid.

320
00:25:37,380 --> 00:25:39,420
She was afraid you might be bored
of the usual dishes that the villagers offer.

321
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:40,220
Oh, yeah!

322
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:43,100
Always Phalo.
My diabetes can't take it anymore.

323
00:25:43,810 --> 00:25:44,860
Oh, wow.

324
00:25:45,050 --> 00:25:47,260
Your mother knows me best.

325
00:25:47,620 --> 00:25:50,020
I can't tell anyone else.

326
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:52,180
You sure had a lot to say earlier!

327
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:56,740
There are so many people here today.

328
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:58,380
Is there some kind of event going on?

329
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:01,620
Oh, there’s no special event or anything.

330
00:26:01,980 --> 00:26:02,980
But look over there.

331
00:26:03,890 --> 00:26:09,100
I heard there are
some political candidates dropping by,

332
00:26:09,220 --> 00:26:12,500
saying they're here to make merit,
pray, and donate money to the temple.

333
00:26:13,250 --> 00:26:15,020
But if you ask me, their main goal.

334
00:26:15,610 --> 00:26:17,100
Is more about campaigning for votes.

335
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:21,020
Donating money
and campaigning at the same time?

336
00:26:22,370 --> 00:26:23,340
Who is that?

337
00:26:24,170 --> 00:26:25,620
I heard his name is Arnon.

338
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:31,580
Luang Por, Today,
I would like to offer some funds to

339
00:26:32,150 --> 00:26:34,340
support the temple and the religion.

340
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:47,340
But I might ask for your permission
to put up a sign in front of the temple.

341
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:49,260
What kind of sign is it?

342
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:52,580
It's a sign with my candidate number
it's not a big one.

343
00:26:53,610 --> 00:26:55,500
I noticed the grass in front
of the temple is quite overgrown.

344
00:26:55,770 --> 00:26:58,100
I'll have my workers
come to clean it up

345
00:26:58,340 --> 00:27:00,740
and repaint the temple's main sign.

346
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:03,820
As long as it doesn't block
or obstruct anything.

347
00:27:03,990 --> 00:27:06,380
And don't trouble the locals,
then go ahead.

348
00:27:06,530 --> 00:27:07,260
Yes.

349
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:09,460
Thank you very much, Luang Por.

350
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:11,740
I’ll be taking my leave now.

351
00:27:18,690 --> 00:27:19,980
Hey.

352
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,220
Oh.

353
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:25,180
Oh, aren't you going to sit?

354
00:27:25,490 --> 00:27:27,860
It's bad karma
to stand over a monk like this.

355
00:27:28,260 --> 00:27:29,300
Is that really okay?

356
00:27:29,530 --> 00:27:31,140
Oh, come on!
You're already here, just sit down.

357
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:40,060
I have so many things to ask you.

358
00:27:40,370 --> 00:27:43,300
Don’t you have anywhere else to be today?

359
00:27:43,770 --> 00:27:46,100
Not at all. I'm free
and can chat for as long as you want.

360
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:47,020
Wow!

361
00:27:47,660 --> 00:27:48,540
Teacher.

362
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:49,780
Are you thirsty?

363
00:27:49,940 --> 00:27:52,220
Then, let me go get
some water for you first.

364
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:54,220
- So we can have a long chat.
- Hey, Singha.

365
00:27:54,340 --> 00:27:55,580
Wait, wait, wait! Hold on.

366
00:27:56,260 --> 00:27:57,260
Look,

367
00:27:57,780 --> 00:28:00,220
If you keep me chatting
for just a little bit longer.

368
00:28:00,890 --> 00:28:02,500
I’m going to miss my lunchtime.

369
00:28:02,770 --> 00:28:04,220
And once that time passes.

370
00:28:04,610 --> 00:28:06,060
I’ll be starving for the rest of the day.

371
00:28:06,340 --> 00:28:08,980
Can you go ask someone else?
Because if you ask me today.

372
00:28:09,220 --> 00:28:11,660
I won't eat again until tomorrow morning

373
00:28:12,340 --> 00:28:13,060
I.

374
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:16,020
I'm not in a hurry at all,
and I still have so many things I want to ask you.

375
00:28:16,370 --> 00:28:17,020
Oh, in a hurry.

376
00:28:17,130 --> 00:28:19,740
And Joe is being so difficult.
he also wanted me to come and ask you.

377
00:28:19,890 --> 00:28:21,860
It's bad enough with just you
asking now Joe has questions for me too?

378
00:28:22,520 --> 00:28:25,020
- No errands either.
- No, I’m free all day.

379
00:28:26,620 --> 00:28:27,900
Do you know Google?

380
00:28:28,770 --> 00:28:31,660
Just type and ask whatever
you want to know. Tell Joe too.

381
00:28:31,970 --> 00:28:34,500
It's almost time! I'm not gonna make it!

382
00:28:34,890 --> 00:28:37,460
- You seem more rushed than I am.
- Yeah.

383
00:28:37,870 --> 00:28:40,180
- Is it because of this fried squid?
- Yeah.

384
00:28:41,380 --> 00:28:42,060
Yep.

385
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:44,820
Okay, I get you now.

386
00:28:45,770 --> 00:28:47,500
- I'm leaving now.
- Ah, okay.

387
00:28:48,420 --> 00:28:49,540
I'll be back.

388
00:28:50,130 --> 00:28:52,420
Come back early tomorrow morning.

389
00:28:55,120 --> 00:28:55,940
Oh.

390
00:28:56,730 --> 00:28:58,940
Is it past noon yet? Oh!

391
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:00,340
Hey Chan.

392
00:29:01,780 --> 00:29:03,380
It’s exactly like you said, man.

393
00:29:03,850 --> 00:29:05,420
It’s so freaking weird, holy shit!

394
00:29:14,050 --> 00:29:14,820
Hello.

395
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:18,260
Sub-Lieutenant Wiriya Krajangwong,
reporting for duty.

396
00:29:25,540 --> 00:29:26,820
Why didn't you go to the police station?

397
00:29:27,410 --> 00:29:29,300
I went there, but the Inspector wasn't there.

398
00:29:29,570 --> 00:29:33,100
They told me the Inspector
was working a case here, so I followed.

399
00:29:34,010 --> 00:29:35,020
We'll talk about that later.

400
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,060
The reason I called you all here today.

401
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,660
Is because I want to show you something.

402
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:57,300
You're not gonna believe this.

403
00:29:59,170 --> 00:30:00,900
The mayor's stomach.

404
00:30:01,410 --> 00:30:03,740
It was full of nothing but alcohol
and a whole pile of hair!

405
00:30:05,260 --> 00:30:08,220
This is so freaking weird.
How the hell did he even eat that?

406
00:30:09,930 --> 00:30:10,860
Inspector,

407
00:30:11,410 --> 00:30:12,420
Excuse me, sir.

408
00:30:20,730 --> 00:30:22,540
Are you saying he was killed by black magic?

409
00:30:23,220 --> 00:30:24,660
But I didn't want to believe it either.

410
00:30:25,770 --> 00:30:27,500
If I hadn't seen it with my own eyes.

411
00:30:27,890 --> 00:30:29,380
And performed the autopsy myself.

412
00:30:29,770 --> 00:30:31,060
I wouldn't believe this shit at all.

413
00:30:31,370 --> 00:30:33,020
I've only ever seen this
in movies or videos.

414
00:30:36,450 --> 00:30:37,540
Then don't believe it just yet!

415
00:30:38,830 --> 00:30:40,340
Find whoever did this.

416
00:30:40,730 --> 00:30:42,220
So we can find out who's behind all this.

417
00:30:43,670 --> 00:30:45,660
I don't even know how to write this report.

418
00:31:13,650 --> 00:31:16,540
Inspector, there’s someone
waiting to see you on the second floor.

419
00:31:19,730 --> 00:31:20,540
Sergeant.

420
00:31:21,350 --> 00:31:23,180
Show the Lieutenant to her desk.

421
00:31:23,690 --> 00:31:24,620
Yes, sir.

422
00:31:24,910 --> 00:31:25,580
Lieutenant,

423
00:31:26,140 --> 00:31:27,260
we'll talk later.

424
00:31:27,810 --> 00:31:28,460
Yes.

425
00:31:29,770 --> 00:31:30,860
- This way, Lieutenant.
- Yes.

426
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:39,660
Greetings, Inspector.

427
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:42,180
I'm Arnon Suphanphon.

428
00:31:42,850 --> 00:31:44,740
Mayoral Candidate Number two.

429
00:31:45,130 --> 00:31:46,260
Running as an independent candidate.

430
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:52,060
I heard that you wanted
to question me further, Inspector.

431
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:54,460
Yes.

432
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:56,660
I appreciate your help with this.

433
00:31:58,340 --> 00:31:59,660
On the night of the incident

434
00:32:00,090 --> 00:32:01,820
- Did Mr. Arnon...
- Excuse me!

435
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:04,340
Before I forget.

436
00:32:05,610 --> 00:32:08,180
I have some bulletproof vests. And...

437
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:11,700
tasers that I'd like to
donate to the station.

438
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,860
And if you're short on anything else,

439
00:32:15,220 --> 00:32:17,380
I can donate directly to the station.

440
00:32:18,280 --> 00:32:19,460
I am more than happy to be of service.

441
00:32:22,460 --> 00:32:23,940
Let's continue.

442
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:28,260
On the night of the incident.

443
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:31,700
before Mayor Akkarapol passed away.

444
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:34,820
what did you talk to him about, Mr. Arnon?

445
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:36,900
And before that.

446
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:39,460
Did you know him personally, Mr. Arnon?

447
00:32:40,850 --> 00:32:41,740
No, I didn't.

448
00:32:44,050 --> 00:32:46,340
I just happened to be having dinner at that hotel.

449
00:32:47,460 --> 00:32:48,700
I saw that he was there.

450
00:32:49,250 --> 00:32:50,260
the number one candidate.

451
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:53,220
So, I just wanted to go over
and pay my respects.

452
00:32:53,730 --> 00:32:54,900
I introduced myself and then left.

453
00:32:55,730 --> 00:32:57,100
That’s all. It was nothing.

454
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:01,620
He was a very generous man.
Very commanding presence.

455
00:33:02,810 --> 00:33:04,180
It's a shame his life was cut a bit short.

456
00:33:06,290 --> 00:33:07,580
But then again, not that short.

457
00:33:08,060 --> 00:33:08,860
He was old.

458
00:33:09,700 --> 00:33:10,900
He's finally at rest now. At rest.

459
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:16,940
And after that?

460
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,900
Where did you go next, Mr. Arnon?

461
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:23,820
I went home to feed my insects.

462
00:33:25,050 --> 00:33:26,100
I keep quite a lot of them.

463
00:33:27,570 --> 00:33:28,860
I love watching them devour their prey.

464
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:30,980
It makes me happy.

465
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,500
Lieutenant, are you ready to get to work?

466
00:34:02,960 --> 00:34:05,300
Then, I need you to dig up
everything you can find on this Mr. Arnon.

467
00:34:05,490 --> 00:34:06,660
I want it in full detail.

468
00:34:07,170 --> 00:34:08,260
Everything else can wait.

469
00:34:09,170 --> 00:34:10,300
Yes, sir.

470
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:17,700
- Arnon.
- Yes.

471
00:34:18,210 --> 00:34:19,500
How’s the election going?

472
00:34:19,970 --> 00:34:20,740
Yes, sir.

473
00:34:21,290 --> 00:34:23,420
In the next election,
whoever your party runs is bound to win anyway.

474
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:25,460
And what about the mafia guys?

475
00:34:26,970 --> 00:34:28,180
It’s all been taken care of.

476
00:34:28,570 --> 00:34:30,900
No problems. But if any come up,
just let me know.

477
00:34:31,810 --> 00:34:34,300
As long as those Russians and
Chinese stay out of it, we’re good.

478
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,940
I’ll deal with them all
at once after the job is done.

479
00:34:38,780 --> 00:34:41,060
Keep my name out of this, you hear me?

480
00:34:41,820 --> 00:34:42,700
Yes.

481
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:44,220
I understand.

482
00:34:55,130 --> 00:34:57,300
Okay, park here.

483
00:35:01,090 --> 00:35:03,060
It was a bumpy ride,
but we're finally here.

484
00:35:04,570 --> 00:35:05,820
Thank you.

485
00:35:09,330 --> 00:35:10,540
Hey, Singha.

486
00:35:13,530 --> 00:35:15,700
I think you should go and
pay your respects to the Buddha."

487
00:35:16,130 --> 00:35:17,460
Your birthday is coming up soon.

488
00:35:18,490 --> 00:35:20,820
they say this year’s
energy is particularly strong.

489
00:35:21,850 --> 00:35:23,700
It’s believed that your 'karmic debtors'

490
00:35:23,820 --> 00:35:25,780
will have full power
to claim what’s owed.

491
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:28,060
Go on, go offer some prayers.

492
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:30,260
And have the Abbot perform
a water blessing for you.

493
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:34,300
Good luck will stay,
and bad luck will turn into a blessing.

494
00:35:35,610 --> 00:35:37,460
I've been through
a lot of bad times already.

495
00:35:38,380 --> 00:35:39,860
I'd better get back to the shop now.

496
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:44,300
It doesn't hurt to believe in this stuff,
you know.

497
00:35:44,970 --> 00:35:46,860
Like they say if you don't believe it,
at least don't disrespect it.

498
00:35:49,270 --> 00:35:50,860
You still don't believe me.

499
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:52,300
Fine.

500
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:54,140
Believe it or not, it's up to you.

501
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:56,220
Drive safely.

502
00:36:34,610 --> 00:36:35,500
Holy shit!

503
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:31,020
That person the one
we performed the ritual for.

504
00:37:31,220 --> 00:37:33,460
I didn't realize
he held such a powerful position.

505
00:37:33,890 --> 00:37:36,820
It’s both risky and difficult.
You need to pay us more.

506
00:37:38,460 --> 00:37:39,740
See? It was worth it.

507
00:37:40,230 --> 00:37:42,580
- Nothing will stand in your way anymore.
- Fine, fine.

508
00:37:43,850 --> 00:37:45,820
How much do you want?
I'll transfer it to you now.

509
00:37:47,330 --> 00:37:49,660
Double the amount.
We'll split it among ourselves.

510
00:37:54,450 --> 00:37:55,460
There’s one more thing.

511
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:59,180
The water ghost I keep it came
and whispered to me.

512
00:38:00,530 --> 00:38:02,900
That someone is keeping a 'Phi Ha'
and it's lurking around this town.

513
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:04,260
Should I take care of it now?

514
00:38:04,890 --> 00:38:06,100
It’s actually quite powerful.

515
00:38:06,690 --> 00:38:08,780
Well, if it gets in our way, deal with it.

516
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:10,180
But it won't be cheap.

517
00:38:13,540 --> 00:38:14,780
Just get lost already.

518
00:38:15,170 --> 00:38:16,860
And don't show your face
around here too often.

519
00:38:24,630 --> 00:38:26,540
Can't all be damn businessmen!

520
00:38:31,370 --> 00:38:32,580
Property in Bang Lamung.

521
00:38:33,530 --> 00:38:34,580
The beachfront plot.

522
00:38:35,160 --> 00:38:36,980
Across from the Laemchabang Hotel.

523
00:38:37,260 --> 00:38:38,340
Sold by owner.

524
00:38:39,620 --> 00:38:40,900
It’s all been cleared up, sir.

525
00:38:41,290 --> 00:38:43,980
We had a proxy do the talking.
We closed the deal at 250 million.

526
00:38:44,450 --> 00:38:45,500
No problems at all.

527
00:38:45,780 --> 00:38:48,100
If anything comes up, just let me know.
MP Banjong.

528
00:38:49,040 --> 00:38:52,140
Keep me out of this.
Destroy all the evidence.

529
00:38:53,650 --> 00:38:54,860
Yes, sir.

530
00:39:05,850 --> 00:39:06,700
Hey!

531
00:39:13,650 --> 00:39:14,780
Did you kill my boss?

532
00:39:15,010 --> 00:39:16,980
Who's your boss?
You’ve got the wrong guy.

533
00:39:17,180 --> 00:39:18,020
Don't say a word.

534
00:39:21,690 --> 00:39:22,500
Go to hell!

535
00:39:23,490 --> 00:39:24,940
- Hey!
- Hey, hurry up!

536
00:39:37,850 --> 00:39:38,660
Where to?

537
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:53,620
Damn it!

538
00:40:15,170 --> 00:40:16,020
Who are you?

539
00:40:22,730 --> 00:40:23,740
We'll talk about it later.

540
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:30,900
Shit! Where the fuck is he?

541
00:40:47,790 --> 00:40:49,300
There are two groups of suspects.

542
00:40:49,650 --> 00:40:51,380
One group assassinated Mr. Arnon.

543
00:40:51,670 --> 00:40:53,420
A stranger appeared,

544
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:56,980
helped Arnon wipe them all out,
then vanished.

545
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:08,700
Wait, Sarge.

546
00:41:09,970 --> 00:41:11,020
Rewind the footage.

547
00:41:11,360 --> 00:41:12,340
Yes, sir.

548
00:41:21,540 --> 00:41:23,260
Wow, that was a direct hit!

549
00:41:24,530 --> 00:41:25,580
He's tough as nails, isn't he?

550
00:41:26,100 --> 00:41:27,300
Is he using black magic or something?

551
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:29,820
Zoom in more, Sarge.

552
00:41:32,860 --> 00:41:33,700
Zoom in again.

553
00:41:36,220 --> 00:41:36,980
More.

554
00:41:40,900 --> 00:41:42,420
Not a single scratch?

555
00:41:42,860 --> 00:41:44,460
What kind of body armor is that?
It’s so thin!

556
00:41:44,770 --> 00:41:47,620
Getting hit by an M4 like that
he should’ve at least been knocked down.

557
00:41:49,050 --> 00:41:50,180
That's the limit, sir.

558
00:41:50,420 --> 00:41:51,540
The image is pixelated now.

559
00:41:52,930 --> 00:41:54,340
Can you make it any clearer?

560
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:58,940
I can't, sir.
This machine has reached its limit.

561
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:01,660
Let me try running it
through the editing rig

562
00:42:01,820 --> 00:42:03,580
and some apps to see what I can do.

563
00:42:03,850 --> 00:42:05,100
It should help a bit.

564
00:42:07,690 --> 00:42:08,460
Hey, Kris!

565
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:10,340
Do you remember that
rubber plantation case in the South?

566
00:42:10,610 --> 00:42:12,220
The one we were assigned to.

567
00:42:12,570 --> 00:42:14,420
"Of course I remember.
How could I forget?

568
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:17,460
How did it go again?

569
00:42:17,900 --> 00:42:20,460
I didn't go in with you
when you raided the place.

570
00:42:21,390 --> 00:42:23,500
Well, at first, we split up
and went in separately.

571
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:25,660
I got to that bastard Chat first.

572
00:42:25,980 --> 00:42:27,060
The bastard actually fought back.

573
00:42:27,570 --> 00:42:29,100
So I emptied the whole clip into him.

574
00:42:29,370 --> 00:42:32,300
By the time I got to him,
the bastard had vanished without a trace.

575
00:42:33,650 --> 00:42:36,340
I saw it with my own eyes.
I shot him right in the chest.

576
00:42:37,130 --> 00:42:38,660
In the end, I just had to
come back and write the report.

577
00:42:39,440 --> 00:42:40,740
No one believed a damn word I said.

578
00:42:41,980 --> 00:42:43,340
In the end, we never caught the bastard.

579
00:42:43,700 --> 00:42:44,980
I've been stuck ever since.

580
00:42:47,210 --> 00:42:48,980
I haven't really followed up
on that case since

581
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:51,620
So, he just vanished?

582
00:42:52,290 --> 00:42:54,780
No. Someone spotted him
all the way down in Nakhon.

583
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:56,860
He was killed by another sorcerer.

584
00:42:57,390 --> 00:42:59,380
They shot him right in the mouth
so he finally died.

585
00:43:00,300 --> 00:43:01,660
But hey, why are you asking?

586
00:43:04,170 --> 00:43:05,780
I’m working on a case right now.

587
00:43:06,180 --> 00:43:07,980
And there are some
strange similarities to that one.

588
00:43:10,290 --> 00:43:11,460
That’s all I wanted to ask.
Sorry to bug you.

589
00:43:11,690 --> 00:43:13,260
I'll give you a call if anything else comes up.

590
00:43:14,460 --> 00:43:15,420
Thank you.

591
00:43:31,300 --> 00:43:32,300
Yeah.

592
00:43:32,930 --> 00:43:35,380
Thank god the 'hero' was here to save me.

593
00:43:35,730 --> 00:43:38,340
A villain like you was absolutely useless.

594
00:43:38,810 --> 00:43:42,300
Hey, Ms. Foon! Open your damn eyes
and look at what this villain is carrying!

595
00:43:42,570 --> 00:43:44,860
This shit is heavy as hell.
You wanna come and carry it for me?

596
00:43:46,110 --> 00:43:48,340
Hey Foon, don't forget.

597
00:43:49,370 --> 00:43:52,100
My mom is going to the temple
to make merit tomorrow morning.

598
00:43:52,610 --> 00:43:54,100
Mom asked you to help set up the shop.

599
00:43:54,260 --> 00:43:55,620
Got it.

600
00:43:56,010 --> 00:43:59,380
Sure thing. I might as well
be your wife at this point.

601
00:43:59,510 --> 00:44:01,700
Oh, dear Singha, my beloved husband.

602
00:44:01,910 --> 00:44:04,340
Sure, make me do all the work,
'dear husband'.

603
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:07,620
Trust me,
Singha doesn't want you as a wife.

604
00:44:07,780 --> 00:44:09,100
Trust me, fucking a sea urchin
or some mud

605
00:44:09,260 --> 00:44:12,180
would be way more fun for him
than being with you.

606
00:44:12,330 --> 00:44:16,220
Wow, look at Mr. Handsome.
Such a hero!

607
00:44:16,370 --> 00:44:18,060
- Thank you.
- Gong Yoo.

608
00:44:18,270 --> 00:44:22,100
Marijoe? Oh, look at you!
So handsome, you dog tick!

609
00:44:22,380 --> 00:44:23,620
You dog tick!

610
00:44:24,340 --> 00:44:27,460
Let's take a photo.
It's been a while, come on!

611
00:44:29,450 --> 00:44:30,740
- Let's put this on socials.
- Sure!

612
00:44:31,410 --> 00:44:33,140
- Socials.
- Socials.

613
00:44:34,980 --> 00:44:36,900
Come on. One, two.

614
00:44:38,100 --> 00:44:38,940
Great.

615
00:44:39,780 --> 00:44:42,740
My hair looks like a rooster.
What the hell is this haircut?

616
00:44:43,100 --> 00:44:44,860
That's just how the sea breeze is.

617
00:44:49,500 --> 00:44:50,540
- Huh.
- Hey.

618
00:44:51,010 --> 00:44:52,220
- What?
- Joe, look at this.

619
00:44:52,450 --> 00:44:53,180
Where?

620
00:44:53,650 --> 00:44:54,460
Here.

621
00:44:54,970 --> 00:44:57,740
Whoa, who's this 'handsome guy' in the glasses?

622
00:44:58,770 --> 00:44:59,740
Here!

623
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:01,420
Behind Singha.

624
00:45:03,050 --> 00:45:03,980
Shit!

625
00:45:04,210 --> 00:45:05,580
Hey, what are you guys
gossiping about me?

626
00:45:06,280 --> 00:45:07,220
What are you guys watching?

627
00:45:08,730 --> 00:45:11,300
- You tell him. You tell Singha yourself!
- Give me that! Let me see.

628
00:45:12,650 --> 00:45:15,180
- Just tell him already!
- Look, it's scary as hell.

629
00:45:24,180 --> 00:45:25,580
You slapped me.

630
00:45:26,450 --> 00:45:28,060
Damn, it's nothing.

631
00:45:28,250 --> 00:45:31,980
The light just hit
your lens. It’s just a reflection.

632
00:45:32,930 --> 00:45:34,340
Are you guys just imagining things?

633
00:45:35,780 --> 00:45:37,460
What kind of fucking ghost
comes out during the day?

634
00:45:38,060 --> 00:45:39,460
There’s something wrong
with your camera.

635
00:45:39,780 --> 00:45:41,580
But I just bought it!

636
00:45:41,820 --> 00:45:43,300
Even ghosts doing overtime
can come out during the day.

637
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:43,940
Night.

638
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:45,860
That shit can show up whenever it wants!

639
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:47,460
- Hey Foon, get over here.
- What? What?

640
00:45:47,590 --> 00:45:49,060
- Send me that photo.
- Why?

641
00:45:49,150 --> 00:45:50,820
- I'm calling P'Jack
- Jack who?

642
00:45:51,050 --> 00:45:52,460
Jack from The Ghost Radio.

643
00:45:52,610 --> 00:45:53,500
Pong?

644
00:45:53,760 --> 00:45:54,540
Are they friends?

645
00:45:54,690 --> 00:45:56,220
- Or do they hate each other?
- They’re having a fight right now.

646
00:45:56,300 --> 00:45:57,220
They’re having a fight now?

647
00:46:12,420 --> 00:46:13,220
Uncle.

648
00:46:28,360 --> 00:46:30,900
This is a Bia Gae.
Keep it on you at all times.

649
00:46:36,850 --> 00:46:38,620
The mercury inside will protect you.

650
00:46:40,930 --> 00:46:42,340
Hurry up and go straight home.

651
00:46:43,370 --> 00:46:44,740
Don't come out if you don't have to.

652
00:46:53,610 --> 00:46:54,340
Uncle.

653
00:46:56,930 --> 00:46:58,140
Is my father still alive?

654
00:47:04,580 --> 00:47:05,860
That's just the karma he has to face.

655
00:47:07,340 --> 00:47:09,740
For people like us,
once we dive into the occult.

656
00:47:10,370 --> 00:47:12,300
the dark arts. black magic.

657
00:47:13,010 --> 00:47:14,540
Once you step into the dark side.

658
00:47:15,260 --> 00:47:16,780
There's no easy way out.

659
00:47:18,780 --> 00:47:20,380
Pull yourself together!

660
00:47:22,790 --> 00:47:24,580
It's getting seriously dangerous lately.

661
00:47:40,010 --> 00:47:41,020
Run away.

662
00:47:42,330 --> 00:47:43,780
Run away.

663
00:47:58,200 --> 00:47:59,020
Father.

664
00:48:00,550 --> 00:48:03,020
Let the Buddha's teachings be your guide.

665
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:06,340
Do only good deeds.

666
00:48:07,470 --> 00:48:09,660
You need to get as far away as possible.

667
00:48:11,050 --> 00:48:12,420
And don't come back.

668
00:48:14,510 --> 00:48:16,940
Someone you love is going to die.

669
00:48:18,400 --> 00:48:20,020
Run away.

670
00:48:23,290 --> 00:48:24,540
Why must I run away? Father?

671
00:48:24,760 --> 00:48:26,780
Why? Why should I be afraid?

672
00:48:28,890 --> 00:48:30,420
Its power is overwhelming.

673
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:34,140
You can't win against it.

674
00:48:36,950 --> 00:48:39,180
It will find you.

675
00:48:40,910 --> 00:48:42,580
It's coming.

676
00:48:45,930 --> 00:48:49,140
Who, Father?
Who’s coming? Tell me who!
